# The pearOS kernel itself isn't installed here: it's a GitHub Release asset
# (too large for apt.pearos.xyz's GitHub Pages hosting), fetched and installed
# in profiles/pear/customize.sh's profile_customize(). linux-libc-dev is the
# regular Debian package, safe to bootstrap normally.
linux-libc-dev
systemd-sysv
udev
apt
iproute2
netbase
procps
bash-completion
sudo
passwd
adduser
initramfs-tools
libpam-modules
util-linux
dbus
# Boot splash engine. The actual pear-plymouth theme ships inside the
# pearos-settings package (PROFILE_REPO_PACKAGES in packages.sh), not here.
# plymouth-themes provides label-pango.so and other rendering plugins the
# theme's .plymouth script needs (without it: "plugin label-pango.so is
# missing" warning and a broken-looking splash).
plymouth
plymouth-themes
# Critical session and permission components
libpam-systemd
polkitd
dbus-user-session
accountsservice
at-spi2-core
libpam-runtime
libnss-systemd
zstd
network-manager
# Plasma Wayland desktop (minimal -- no X11 server/session)
sddm
plasma-desktop
plasma-workspace
kwin-wayland
kscreen
upower
powerdevil
plasma-vault
plasma-pa
bluedevil
print-manager
plasma-nm
xdg-desktop-portal-kde
xdg-desktop-portal
xdg-user-dirs
xdg-utils
breeze-gtk-theme
xwayland
nautilus
konsole
kate
ark
gnome-maps
gwenview
elisa
kdeconnect
# Bootloader and Disk. Ploader is vendored under profiles/<name>/ploader/
# (not a package) and is live-USB only -- isolinux/syslinux-common just
# provide the BIOS boot binaries Phase 7 copies out of this chroot for the
# ISO itself. grub-efi-amd64-bin/grub-pc are for the INSTALLED system:
# Calamares' stock "bootloader" module runs grub-install/update-grub on
# the target after Calamares copies this chroot to disk, so those need to
# actually exist here even though nothing in the live session uses them.
isolinux
syslinux-common
efibootmgr
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-pc
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
# Theming tooling
# kdeglobals ships widgetStyle=kvantum-dark, needing the Kvantum engine itself
qt-style-kvantum
# pafari's postinst runs glib-compile-schemas -- that binary is in
# libglib2.0-bin ("Programs for the GLib library"), not libglib2.0-dev-bin
# ("Development utilities", gdbus-codegen/glib-compile-resources -- nothing
# we ship calls those). The dev package was in here instead, so the schema
# compile step was silently failing (swallowed by `|| true` in the postinst).
libglib2.0-bin
ca-certificates
wget
curl
unzip
# pearOS-installer (cloned in customize.sh) is a Python/GTK4 app
python3-gi
python3-gi-cairo
gir1.2-gtk-4.0
# gtkapp's wallpaper/liquid_gel/svgpath modules use numpy for array math
python3-numpy
# post-install's finish page shells out to qrencode when post_setup fails,
# to turn the crash log (or a link to it, if online) into a scannable QR
# code -- curl (already above) does the paste upload half of that
qrencode
# pearos-zshconfig's .zshrc sources zsh-autosuggestions directly and shells
# out to `last` (moved from util-linux to wtmpdb on modern Debian) for a
# login banner -- needs all three or shells fail to start
zsh
zsh-autosuggestions
wtmpdb
# wtmpdb alone only tracks boot/shutdown (wtmpdb-update-boot.service) --
# without this, no PAM hook actually records logins, so `last <user>` is
# always empty regardless. Debian's libpam-* packages self-register via
# pam-auth-update in their postinst, no manual /etc/pam.d edit needed.
libpam-wtmpdb
# Browser and Multimedia
vlc
# Flatpak support
flatpak
gnome-software
